---
source: tests/cli.rs
expression: "help_output(&[\"--help\"])"
---
Manage canonical AI skill stores, materialise configured skill view symlinks, and record calibration data for multi-phase-plan.

Usage: skillnet [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  status        Show scope divergence and catalog health
  doctor        Check configured scopes for invariant violations
  completions   Generate shell completion scripts
  view          Materialise and inspect global view symlinks
  sync          Materialise every configured global view and project view in one shot
  export        Export repo-stored skills into the configured global skill store
  config        Manage skillnet's configuration files
  project       Manage configured project roots
  subscription  Sync subscribed skill repositories into local skill directories
  skill         List, inspect, and edit mirrored skill directories
  scope         Inspect configured canonical scopes
  catalog       Generate and validate skill catalog metadata
  template      Preview model-bound skill templates
  models        Inspect cached T3 provider models
  calibration   Record and verify multi-phase-plan calibration data
  hook          Ingest shell hook payloads
  usage         Record and report normalized skill usage

Options:
      --config <CONFIG>
          Path to the skillnet TOML configuration file

          [env: SKILLNET_CONFIG=]

      --mirror-root <MIRROR_ROOT>
          Root directory containing the global skill mirror directory

          [env: SKILLNET_MIRROR_ROOT=]

      --catalog-config <CATALOG_CONFIG>
          Path to the skill catalog metadata configuration file

          [env: SKILLNET_CATALOG_CONFIG=]

      --database-url <URL>
          Postgres URL for the calibration database

      --dry-run
          Print planned filesystem changes without mutating files

      --allow-dirty-destination
          Allow mutating the mirror destination even when its Git working tree is dirty

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
